{
    "@context": "https://schema.org/",
    "@type": "BlogPosting",
    "@id": "https://www.midwest-tropical.com/decorating-around-indoor-water-features-to-enhance-look/#BlogPosting",
    "url": "https://www.midwest-tropical.com/decorating-around-indoor-water-features-to-enhance-look/",
    "inLanguage": "en-US",
    "mainEntityOfPage": "https://www.midwest-tropical.com/decorating-around-indoor-water-features-to-enhance-look/",
    "headline": "Stylish Decor Ideas to Enhance Indoor Water Features",
    "description": "Transform indoor spaces into peaceful oases with elegant water features, creating welcoming and joyful environments. Whether it's a soothing water wall or...",
    "articleBody": "Water features bring a sense of tranquility and elegance to indoor spaces, transforming them into welcoming and happy places. Whether you have a water wall, bubble wall, fountain, rain wall, or wall fountain, these are themselves pretty unique features, but decorating around them can improve the whole look of the place even more.    Bubble Walls:\u0026nbsp;    Bubbles take us to the cartoonish world. Having\u0026nbsp;bubble water features\u0026nbsp;adds a playful and hypnotizing element to interior design, with bubbles dancing behind a transparent panel. Since bubbles are initially found in nature, add some natural elements along your bubble walls, like pairing them with colorful plants and accent furniture with decorative pillows to create a cheerful atmosphere. To balance the visual delight, anchor the space with neutral rugs or flooring and minimalist wall decor.    Wall Fountains:\u0026nbsp;    Wall fountains fill spaces with the calming sound of water flowing, creating a peaceful aura in any room. When decorating around them, go for a harmonious look according to the\u0026nbsp;wall waterfall design.\u0026nbsp;Choose furniture with geometrical lines and organic shapes to complement the gentle curves of the wall. Add natural items like wood or stone accents, plants, or even fish to bring nature indoors and make a connection to the outdoors.    You can also add sculptures and tables around it with scented candles and magazines for sophistication.    Water Walls:\u0026nbsp;    So, your office has water walls? They can create a captivating focal point in any room, with cascading water working like a personal soundtrack of the room. But you should also decorate around them. To create a contemporary aesthetic, consider items that complement its natural elegance with minimalist decor, like sleek furniture pieces, modern sofas, or streamlined chairs. You can also add minimalistic lighting that puts the spotlight on the water wall.    Glass Water Walls:\u0026nbsp;    Glass water walls offer a smooth blend of sophistication and tranquility, with water flowing gracefully and calmly through a transparent surface ?making the water seem like it's floating. When decorating around it, focus on creating an elegant and sophisticated look, like\u0026nbsp;a glass water feature wall. Choose luxurious-looking materials like marble or granite for countertops to complement the feature (you can have your restaurant's reception in front of a glass wall with a black granite counter in front).    Apart from this, add luxurious seating options, like velvet armchairs or leather sofas, to add a touch of lavishness to the space. Don't forget to add soft and warm lights to complete the look.    Conclusion    We know that water features are enough in themselves when it comes to decoration, but sometimes, they look incomplete without decorations around them. That is why it doesn't matter what type of water feature your commercial space has; you can always add furniture pieces, plants, or sculptures around it to boost its look.    However, remember never to overpower your focal point, the water feature. All your d?cor should complete the feature but never take over it.",
